     "\r\n<font face=\"tahoma\" size=\"2\"><p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:tahoma;font-size:10pt\"><span>Dear colleagues,</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:tahoma;font-size:10pt\"><span>We are pleased to announce the online course </span><strong><span>Introduction to Occupancy Models with R</span></strong><span>, taking place </span><strong><span>1–4 December</span></strong><span>.</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:tahoma;font-size:10pt\"> </p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:tahoma;font-size:10pt\"><span>Course website: <a href=\"https://www.physalia-courses.org/courses-workshops/occupancymodels/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" title=\"This external link will open in a new window\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.physalia-courses.org/courses-workshops/occupancymodels/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792447745442000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2P3Oe23X9vgW7DOIeN8kEb\">https://www.physalia-courses.org/courses-workshops/occupancymodels/</a> </span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:tahoma;font-size:10pt\"> </p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:tahoma;font-size:10pt\"> </p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:tahoma;font-size:10pt\"><span>This\r\n practical workshop will introduce participants to occupancy modelling \r\nin R, with a focus on imperfect detection, repeated \r\ndetection–non-detection data, ecological and survey covariates, \r\npredictions, model assessment, and reproducible workflows.</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:tahoma;font-size:10pt\"><span>Participants will work with the </span><strong><span>tsoccu</span></strong><span> and </span><strong><span>unmarked</span></strong><span> packages through live coding demonstrations, practical exercises, and ecological case studies.</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:tahoma;font-size:10pt\"> </p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:tahoma;font-size:10pt\"><strong><span>No prior knowledge of occupancy models is required.</span></strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:tahoma;font-size:10pt\"> </p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:tahoma;font-size:10pt\"> </p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:tahoma;font-size:10pt\"><span>Best regards,</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:tahoma;font-size:10pt\"> </p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:tahoma;font-size:10pt\"><span>Carlo</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:tahoma;font-size:10pt\"> </p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:tahoma;font-size:10pt\"> </p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:tahoma;font-size:10pt\"> </p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:tahoma;font-size:10pt\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma;font-size:small\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma;font-size:small\"></span></span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:trebuchet ms;font-size:10pt\">--------------------<br><br>Carlo Pecoraro, Ph.D<br><br><br>Physalia-courses DIRECTOR<br><br><a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">in...@physalia-courses.org</a></p></font>\r\n\r\n"
